WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.970 line:0%
<i> An ancient arena
 for ocean giants.</i>

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.307 line:0%
(music)

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:12.611 line:0%
<i> In one corner,
 enormous yellowfin tuna,</i>

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:14.847 line:0%
<i> nearly twice the length
 of a man,</i>

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.483 line:0%
<i> weighing over 800 pounds.</i>

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:20.453 line:0%
<i> One of the fastest fish
 in the ocean.</i>

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:25.291 line:0%
<i> In the other corner,
 sharks; thousands of them.</i>

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.095 line:0%
<i> Crushing teeth,</i>

00:00:30.095 --> 00:00:33.399 line:0%
<i> lightning-fast speed,</i>

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:37.003 line:0%
<i> and street-gang numbers.</i>

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:40.840 line:0%
<i> But the tuna remain
 one step ahead.</i>

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.944 line:0%
<i> This is</i> Shark vs. Tuna.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:48.381 line:0%
(music)

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:55.288 line:0%
(music)

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:57.791 line:0%
<i> Some call it The Rock.</i>

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:04.697 line:0%
<i> A Jurassic Park lost
 in the South Atlantic Ocean.</i>

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:12.738 line:0%
<i> Over 1,000 miles from land
 in any direction,</i>

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:17.443 line:0%
<i> this is Ascension Island,</i>

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:20.346 line:0%
<i> Darwin's best-kept secret.</i>

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.886 line:0%
<i> Everything that lives here
 or stops here</i>

00:01:27.886 --> 00:01:31.091 line:0%
<i> is either hunter or hunted.</i>

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:37.730 line:0%
<i> Ascension plays host to one
 of nature's greatest showdowns.</i>

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.067 line:0%
<i> Thousands of the ocean's
 most deadly predators</i>

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.269 line:0%
<i> arrive from far and wide</i>

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:48.007 line:0%
<i> to fight it out in
 a high-stakes battle royale.</i>

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:52.178 line:0%
(music)

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:58.217 line:0%
(music)

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:01.821 line:0%
<i> Schools of jacks
 dominate the drop-offs.</i>

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.258 line:0%
<i> Thousands of green turtles
 come here annually</i>

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:09.295 line:0%
<i> to nest on the sandy beaches,</i>

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.432 line:0%
<i> and swarms of huge
 predatory fish</i>

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:17.704 line:0%
<i> like barracuda, marlin and
 wahoo lurk in the open water.</i>

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.774 line:0%
<i> But no one is safe.</i>

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:31.184 line:0%
<i> Except maybe this
 enormous yellowfin tuna.</i>

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.853 line:0%
<i> This super fish
 normally lives life</i>

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:38.358 line:0%
<i> in the desert of the open ocean
 where food is scarce.</i>

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.295 line:0%
<i> But every Easter,</i>

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:46.431 line:0%
<i> Ascension Island becomes
 an oasis for giant tuna</i>

00:02:46.431 --> 00:02:48.968 line:0%
<i> migrating across the Atlantic.</i>

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.305 line:0%
<i> It's one of the largest
 concentrations</i>

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:55.941 line:0%
<i> of yellowfin in the world.</i>

00:02:55.941 --> 00:03:01.881 line:0%
(music)

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:05.184 line:0%
<i> To get in and out
 of The Rock alive,</i>

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.888 line:0%
<i> you must be big,
 smart and fast.</i>

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.027 line:0%
<i> Despite being near the top
 of the food chain,</i>

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:18.297 line:0%
<i> tuna are a favorite meal
 for sharks,</i>

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:20.099 line:0%
<i> if they can catch them.</i>

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:24.136 line:0%
<i> So not only must the yellowfin
 be an exceptional predator,</i>

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:26.906 line:0%
<i> it must be a wily
 escape artist, too.</i>

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:32.445 line:0%
<i> The average yellowfin
 is by no means small,</i>

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:36.949 line:0%
<i> but Ascension is
 home to giants.</i>

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:39.485 line:0%
<i> Nearly twice
 the length of a man</i>

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.288 line:0%
<i> and as heavy as a horse,</i>

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.323 line:0%
<i> this is one of the fastest fish</i>

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.625 line:0%
<i> in the ocean.</i>

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:48.561
<i> Even the US Navy studied it as</i>

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.364
<i> a model for submersible drones.</i>

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.733
<i> Built for speed,</i>

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:56.168
<i> the tuna's gills are over</i>

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:57.737
<i> 30 times larger than</i>

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.404
<i> other fish its size,</i>

00:03:59.404 --> 00:04:02.975
<i> to draw in more oxygen.</i>

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:04.644
<i> And its heart is 10 times</i>

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:08.680
<i> bigger with a faster heartbeat.</i>

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.449
<i> Like the great white shark,</i>

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:12.718
<i> the yellowfin is warm-blooded,</i>

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:15.387
<i> which allows it to swim
 faster for longer</i>

00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:16.355
<i> and exploit the colder,</i>

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:17.757 line:0%
<i> deeper waters</i>

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:20.159 line:0%
<i> where other predators
 can't hunt.</i>

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:26.833
<i> Little can keep up with or
 escape this turbocharged fish.</i>

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:34.974 line:0%
<i> And their next feeding stop
 is Ascension Island.</i>

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:39.512 line:0%
(music)

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:43.282 line:0%
<i> The tuna's arrival
 acts like a dinner bell</i>

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:46.619 line:0%
<i> for some of the ocean's
 fiercest marine predators.</i>

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:51.724 line:0%
<i> At this time of year,</i>

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:55.428 line:0%
<i> the tuna are set to run
 a gauntlet of sharks.</i>

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:02.201 line:0%
<i> And they aren't the only ones
 that want a piece of the tuna.</i>

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:08.875 line:0%
(music)

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.277 line:0%
<i> Tales of Ascension's
 big game fish</i>

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:14.013 line:0%
<i> attract sports fishermen
 and trophy hunters</i>

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.915 line:0%
<i> from all over the world.</i>

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.920 line:0%
<i> Of all the fish
 they target here,</i>

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.625 line:0%
<i> the giant yellowfin
 is highly prized.</i>

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:31.331 line:0%
<i> Some carry a $20,000 paycheck.</i>

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:40.372 line:0%
<i> The wily tuna doesn't take
 the bait this time;</i>

00:05:40.372 --> 00:05:43.442 line:0%
<i> an eight-foot wahoo does.</i>

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:45.277 line:0%
(music)

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:51.717 line:0%
(music)

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:58.256 line:0%
(music)

00:05:58.256 --> 00:06:02.962 line:0%
<i> Below the surface, the fish's
 struggles are a call to arms.</i>

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:07.866 line:0%
(music)

00:06:07.866 --> 00:06:10.669 line:0%
<i> At Ascension,
 everyone's hungry.</i>

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:16.742 line:0%
(music)

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:23.182 line:0%
(music)

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:29.622 line:0%
(music)

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:36.061 line:0%
(music)

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:42.668 line:0%
(music)

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:49.609 line:0%
(music)

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:55.180 line:0%
<i> In under a minute, a 120-pound
 wahoo is obliterated.</i>

00:06:55.180 --> 00:07:02.254 line:0%
(music)

00:07:02.254 --> 00:07:06.959 line:0%
<i> They try to eat everything,
 even the bony head.</i>

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:10.129 line:0%
(music)

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:16.568 line:0%
(music)

00:07:16.568 --> 00:07:23.475 line:0%
(music)

00:07:23.475 --> 00:07:30.449 line:0%
(music)

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.918 line:0%
<i> With the sharks
 distracted in frenzy,</i>

00:07:32.918 --> 00:07:35.187 line:0%
<i> the tuna escape,</i>

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:37.790 line:0%
<i> but the battle lines are drawn.</i>

00:07:39.257 --> 00:07:42.094 line:0%
<i> These sharks mean business,</i>

00:07:42.094 --> 00:07:44.096 line:0%
<i> and there are
 thousands of them.</i>

00:07:56.442 --> 00:08:00.178 line:0%
<i> Like the tuna, sharks ride
 the South Atlantic current</i>

00:08:00.178 --> 00:08:03.515 line:0%
<i> to Ascension
 in terrifying numbers.</i>

00:08:03.515 --> 00:08:09.455 line:0%
(music)

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:12.758 line:0%
<i> Tigers, hammerheads and mako,</i>

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:18.197 line:0%
<i> to the ever-increasing
 sightings of Galapagos sharks,</i>

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:21.067 line:0%
<i> each is locked in
 an evolutionary arms race</i>

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:23.402 line:0%
<i> with the tuna.</i>

00:08:23.402 --> 00:08:27.240 line:0%
<i> And right now,
 no one knows who's winning.</i>

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:34.013 line:0%
<i> The sharks patrol the beaches.</i>

00:08:36.715 --> 00:08:39.585 line:0%
<i> The Rock is under siege.</i>

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:44.590 line:0%
(music)

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:50.462 line:0%
(music)

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:54.099 line:0%
<i> There is an abundance
 of prey here,</i>

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:55.601 line:0%
<i> but like the fishermen,</i>

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:59.505 line:0%
<i> the sharks' holy grail
 is the giant yellowfin.</i>

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:05.644 line:0%
<i> After traveling thousands
 of miles to get here,</i>

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:09.948 line:0%
<i> these sharks are desperate
 to replenish their reserves.</i>

00:09:09.948 --> 00:09:13.552 line:0%
(music)

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:18.657 line:0%
(music)

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:21.459 line:0%
<i> Tuna are jam-packed
 with some of the richest,</i>

00:09:21.459 --> 00:09:24.964 line:0%
<i> fattiest meat in the ocean,</i>

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:29.435 line:0%
<i> and an 800-pound yellowfin
 is the jackpot.</i>

00:09:33.271 --> 00:09:36.341 line:0%
<i> But how on Earth will these
 sharks successfully catch</i>

00:09:36.341 --> 00:09:39.945 line:0%
<i> and kill such formidable prey?</i>

00:09:39.945 --> 00:09:45.651 line:0%
(music)

00:09:45.651 --> 00:09:51.123 line:0%
<i> Yellowfin tuna are unbelievably
 fast, powerful predators,</i>

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:56.328 line:0%
<i> and for a shark,
 incredibly hard to catch.</i>

00:09:56.328 --> 00:09:58.330 line:0%
<i> There are only
 a handful of contenders</i>

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:02.000 line:0%
<i> up for the tuna challenge.</i>

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.102 line:0%
<i> To hunt these super fish,</i>

00:10:04.102 --> 00:10:07.273 line:0%
<i> you need extraordinary
 predatory powers.</i>

00:10:11.543 --> 00:10:15.982 line:0%
<i> Meet the resident bad boy,
 the Galapagos shark.</i>

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:22.588 line:0%
<i> Ascension is their
 local hunting ground,</i>

00:10:22.588 --> 00:10:25.657 line:0%
<i> and unlike the tuna
 and migrant sharks,</i>

00:10:25.657 --> 00:10:29.362 line:0%
<i> they know this terrain like
 the backs of their hands.</i>

00:10:31.663 --> 00:10:33.665 line:0%
<i> Most of them grew up here,</i>

00:10:33.665 --> 00:10:37.135 line:0%
<i> learning to hunt
 in the shallow nurseries.</i>

00:10:37.135 --> 00:10:39.171 line:0%
<i> And in the last two years,</i>

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:42.041 line:0%
<i> Galapagos sightings have
 increased dramatically.</i>

00:10:43.542 --> 00:10:46.144
<i> Despite reaching
 12 feet in length,</i>

00:10:46.144 --> 00:10:48.446
<i> this welterweight is
 only half the size</i>

00:10:48.446 --> 00:10:50.682 line:0%
<i> of the giant yellowfin.</i>

00:10:50.682 --> 00:10:52.817 line:0%
<i> Its streamlined
 and slender frame</i>

00:10:52.817 --> 00:10:54.720 line:0%
<i> does give this shark agility</i>

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.322
<i> and speed like the tuna,</i>

00:10:57.322 --> 00:10:59.992
<i> but like its cousin,
 the tiger shark,</i>

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:03.028 line:0%
<i> the Galapagos has
 more powerful jaws</i>

00:11:03.028 --> 00:11:05.731 line:0%
<i> and sharper, serrated teeth.</i>

00:11:07.866 --> 00:11:10.402 line:0%
<i> This allows for
 a highly varied diet,</i>

00:11:10.402 --> 00:11:13.939 line:0%
<i> from bony fish and iguanas,
 to sea lions,</i>

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:16.375 line:0%
<i> and even each other.</i>

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:20.746 line:0%
<i> But here at Ascension,</i>

00:11:20.746 --> 00:11:24.216 line:0%
<i> yellowfin remain
 a number one prize.</i>

00:11:26.285 --> 00:11:29.487 line:0%
<i> Oily prey like tuna
 leaves a scent signature</i>

00:11:29.487 --> 00:11:33.291 line:0%
<i> up to two miles away.</i>

00:11:33.291 --> 00:11:35.127 line:0%
<i> In the open blue water,</i>

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:38.430 line:0%
<i> this Galapagos shark's
 incredible sense of smell</i>

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:42.234 line:0%
<i> could give it the edge.</i>

00:11:42.234 --> 00:11:46.571 line:0%
<i> Almost two-thirds of their
 brain is dedicated to smell.</i>

00:11:46.571 --> 00:11:50.876 line:0%
(music)

00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:56.548 line:0%
<i> The nostrils, or nares,
 are not required for breathing.</i>

00:11:56.548 --> 00:11:59.751 line:0%
<i> All the better
 to smell you with.</i>

00:11:59.751 --> 00:12:02.955 line:0%
<i> 10,000 times better
 than humans.</i>

00:12:04.857 --> 00:12:10.829 line:0%
<i> Where the Galapagos shark
 matches the tuna is in numbers.</i>

00:12:10.829 --> 00:12:15.701 line:0%
<i> Most sharks hunt alone, but
 the Galapagos move in a mob,</i>

00:12:15.701 --> 00:12:18.604 line:0%
<i> a veritable street gang
 of aggression.</i>

00:12:22.775 --> 00:12:27.079 line:0%
<i> They investigate anything that
 may potentially become prey.</i>

00:12:30.349 --> 00:12:32.183 line:0%
<i> Like a school of piranhas,</i>

00:12:32.183 --> 00:12:36.054 line:0%
<i> competition drives them
 to frenzy.</i>

00:12:36.054 --> 00:12:39.057 line:0%
(music)

00:12:39.057 --> 00:12:44.830 line:0%
(music)

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:49.067 line:0%
<i> The Galapagos may be
 fast, agile and aggressive,</i>

00:12:49.067 --> 00:12:51.236 line:0%
<i> and they may have the numbers,</i>

00:12:51.236 --> 00:12:55.141 line:0%
<i> but one-on-one,
 they hardly stand a chance.</i>

00:12:57.109 --> 00:12:58.477 line:0%
<i> In the open ocean,</i>

00:12:58.477 --> 00:13:01.379 line:0%
<i> the giant tuna
 are just too fast,</i>

00:13:01.379 --> 00:13:04.283 line:0%
<i> too strong and too big.</i>

00:13:06.185 --> 00:13:09.854 line:0%
<i> This underdog would have to do
 something spectacular</i>

00:13:09.854 --> 00:13:12.558 line:0%
<i> to sink its teeth into one.</i>

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:19.732 line:0%
<i> To win a giant tuna, you need
 to put more on the table.</i>

00:13:21.966 --> 00:13:25.070 line:0%
<i> A heavyweight enters the ring.</i>

00:13:26.938 --> 00:13:29.108 line:0%
<i> The tiger shark.</i>

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:35.181 line:0%
<i> Like its namesake, its striped
 camouflage allows the tiger</i>

00:13:35.181 --> 00:13:39.485 line:0%
<i> to silently stalk prey,
 virtually undetected.</i>

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:48.426 line:0%
<i> Their stripes
 may fade with age,</i>

00:13:48.426 --> 00:13:51.764 line:0%
<i> but killer instincts
 and voracious appetites</i>

00:13:51.764 --> 00:13:54.366 line:0%
<i> stay with them for life.</i>

00:13:54.366 --> 00:13:56.668 line:0%
(music)

00:13:56.668 --> 00:14:03.375 line:0%
(music)

00:14:03.375 --> 00:14:07.112
<i> This undisputed heavyweight
 weighs nearly four times more</i>

00:14:07.112 --> 00:14:09.514
<i> than the giant tuna</i>

00:14:09.514 --> 00:14:10.849
<i> and reaches over half</i>

00:14:10.849 --> 00:14:12.985
<i> the length of a school bus.</i>

00:14:15.754 --> 00:14:19.992 line:0%
<i> It has an arsenal of weaponry</i>

00:14:19.992 --> 00:14:24.830 line:0%
<i> to track, hunt and devour
 massive prey.</i>

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:33.471 line:0%
<i> These super-fast yellowfins
 are no easy target,</i>

00:14:33.471 --> 00:14:35.608 line:0%
<i> so the tiger shark
 will be on the lookout</i>

00:14:35.608 --> 00:14:40.279 line:0%
<i> for struggling young,
 injured and old fish.</i>

00:14:43.482 --> 00:14:46.418 line:0%
<i> A large school offers
 safety in numbers,</i>

00:14:46.418 --> 00:14:51.456 line:0%
<i> both to hunt and
 to keep a lookout,</i>

00:14:51.456 --> 00:14:54.994 line:0%
<i> but you can't hide
 from the tiger shark.</i>

00:14:57.229 --> 00:15:01.400 line:0%
<i> Two powerful internal ears
 in its forehead pick up sound</i>

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:05.136 line:0%
<i> from several miles away,</i>

00:15:05.136 --> 00:15:08.107 line:0%
<i> while specialized
 reflective plates in the eyes</i>

00:15:08.107 --> 00:15:11.643 line:0%
<i> provide night vision
 in low light.</i>

00:15:11.643 --> 00:15:16.714 line:0%
<i> And even if the tiger can't
 see, smell or hear its prey,</i>

00:15:16.714 --> 00:15:19.285 line:0%
<i> it can still feel them.</i>

00:15:21.186 --> 00:15:25.190
<i> Tracing the shark's body is
 a thin, fluid-filled tube</i>

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.793
<i> known as the lateral line.</i>

00:15:27.793 --> 00:15:31.997
<i> Like an ear, it's lined
 with millions of tiny hairs</i>

00:15:31.997 --> 00:15:35.000 line:0%
<i> that react to any movement
 in the water,</i>

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:39.404 line:0%
<i> the kind of movement
 created by feeding tunas.</i>

00:15:39.404 --> 00:15:45.343 line:0%
(music)

00:15:45.343 --> 00:15:48.280 line:0%
<i> This built-in tracking device
 helps distinguish</i>

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:52.617 line:0%
<i> large from small prey,
 individual from school,</i>

00:15:52.617 --> 00:15:56.421 line:0%
<i> as well as the distance
 and speed of its target.</i>

00:15:56.421 --> 00:16:02.928 line:0%
(music)

00:16:02.928 --> 00:16:05.464 line:0%
<i> Once the tiger
 gets within range,</i>

00:16:05.464 --> 00:16:08.434 line:0%
<i> the tuna doesn't
 stand a chance.</i>

00:16:12.738 --> 00:16:17.008 line:0%
<i> This juggernaut has the power
 to crush a car.</i>

00:16:17.008 --> 00:16:19.444 line:0%
(music)

00:16:19.444 --> 00:16:24.949 line:0%
(music)

00:16:24.949 --> 00:16:30.855 line:0%
<i> It can eat anything,
 from dolphins, rays and seals,</i>

00:16:30.855 --> 00:16:33.859 line:0%
<i> to whatever falls
 into the water,</i>

00:16:33.859 --> 00:16:39.097 line:0%
<i> like birds, trash
 and even people.</i>

00:16:39.097 --> 00:16:40.966 line:0%
<i> The tiger shark is responsible</i>

00:16:40.966 --> 00:16:45.737 line:0%
<i> for the most attacks
 against humans,</i>

00:16:45.737 --> 00:16:48.340 line:0%
<i> second only to the great white.</i>

00:16:52.377 --> 00:16:55.613 line:0%
<i> This indiscriminate diet
 is largely thanks</i>

00:16:55.613 --> 00:17:00.218 line:0%
<i> to their highly
 specialized teeth.</i>

00:17:00.218 --> 00:17:03.088 line:0%
<i> This turtle, which
 most likely succumbed</i>

00:17:03.088 --> 00:17:05.190 line:0%
<i> to the exhaustion of nesting,</i>

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:07.926 line:0%
<i> may be too tough
 for most sharks,</i>

00:17:07.926 --> 00:17:11.830 line:0%
<i> but for the tiger,
 it's a welcome meal.</i>

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:15.267 line:0%
(music)

00:17:15.267 --> 00:17:21.706 line:0%
(music)

00:17:21.706 --> 00:17:25.978 line:0%
(music)

00:17:28.647 --> 00:17:32.150
<i> Unlike other sharks that have
 a variety of teeth,</i>

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.853
<i> the tigers are
 almost identical,</i>

00:17:34.853 --> 00:17:39.157
<i> each working like
 a circular saw.</i>

00:17:39.157 --> 00:17:43.361 line:0%
<i> The highly-serrated edge
 cuts and slices through flesh,</i>

00:17:43.361 --> 00:17:47.699 line:0%
<i> and the large, razor-sharp cusp
 hacks through bone and shell</i>

00:17:47.699 --> 00:17:50.602 line:0%
<i> while the curved shape
 helps brace each tooth</i>

00:17:50.602 --> 00:17:52.771 line:0%
<i> against the powerful bite.</i>

00:17:55.073 --> 00:17:58.443 line:0%
<i> The tiger pulverizes
 the turtle's bones and shell</i>

00:17:58.443 --> 00:18:01.780 line:0%
<i> to unlock marrow,
 proteins and fats.</i>

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:07.618 line:0%
(music)

00:18:07.618 --> 00:18:11.189 line:0%
<i> It's all tasty nutrition...</i>

00:18:11.189 --> 00:18:13.558 line:0%
<i> if you've got
 the stomach for it.</i>

00:18:13.558 --> 00:18:16.061 line:0%
(music)

00:18:16.061 --> 00:18:22.867 line:0%
(music)

00:18:22.867 --> 00:18:27.506 line:0%
<i> The tiger's oversized gut is
 lined with a muscular wall</i>

00:18:27.506 --> 00:18:32.377 line:0%
<i> nearly three times thicker
 than other sharks'</i>

00:18:32.377 --> 00:18:36.982 line:0%
<i> and filled with enough acid
 to handle a license plate.</i>

00:18:38.817 --> 00:18:42.321 line:0%
<i> The giant yellowfin
 may be a prize catch,</i>

00:18:42.321 --> 00:18:45.824 line:0%
<i> but this scavenger can fill up
 on any available food source</i>

00:18:45.824 --> 00:18:48.494 line:0%
<i> it finds at Ascension.</i>

00:18:51.829 --> 00:18:54.299 line:0%
<i> Yet despite all its raw power,</i>

00:18:54.299 --> 00:18:58.837 line:0%
<i> the tiger shark isn't fast
 enough to catch a healthy tuna.</i>

00:18:58.837 --> 00:19:03.241 line:0%
(music)

00:19:03.241 --> 00:19:06.611 line:0%
<i> This tank can only swim
 slightly faster</i>

00:19:06.611 --> 00:19:08.814 line:0%
<i> than an iceberg.</i>

00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:12.183 line:0%
<i> Even at its top speed
 of 20 miles per hour,</i>

00:19:12.183 --> 00:19:15.320 line:0%
<i> it doesn't have
 the stamina to keep up.</i>

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:20.392 line:0%
(music)

00:19:20.392 --> 00:19:23.861 line:0%
<i> To catch these fish,
 you need real speed,</i>

00:19:23.861 --> 00:19:27.266 line:0%
<i> and there is only
 one shark fast enough.</i>

00:19:33.672 --> 00:19:35.306 line:0%
<i> As well as numbers,</i>

00:19:35.306 --> 00:19:39.211 line:0%
<i> the tuna also have exceptional
 speed and endurance.</i>

00:19:40.846 --> 00:19:43.648 line:0%
<i> Thanks to their
 fatigue-resistant muscles,</i>

00:19:43.648 --> 00:19:46.618 line:0%
<i> the giant tuna could finish
 the Boston Marathon</i>

00:19:46.618 --> 00:19:50.988 line:0%
<i> in just over 30 minutes,</i>

00:19:50.988 --> 00:19:54.459 line:0%
<i> maxing out at
 up to 47 miles per hour,</i>

00:19:54.459 --> 00:19:57.262 line:0%
<i> as fast as an American
 quarter horse.</i>

00:19:59.164 --> 00:20:00.898
<i> Maneuvering at such pace</i>

00:20:00.898 --> 00:20:04.169
<i> requires military precision.</i>

00:20:04.169 --> 00:20:08.773
<i> The tuna's bright yellow
 finlets help reduce turbulence</i>

00:20:08.773 --> 00:20:10.342
<i> while its fins retract</i>

00:20:10.342 --> 00:20:15.179 line:0%
<i> into modified grooves
 to minimize drag.</i>

00:20:15.179 --> 00:20:17.582 line:0%
<i> And unlike any other creature,</i>

00:20:17.582 --> 00:20:21.453 line:0%
<i> the tuna uses its lymphatic
 system like hydraulics</i>

00:20:21.453 --> 00:20:23.087 line:0%
<i> to stiffen its fins,</i>

00:20:23.087 --> 00:20:24.856 line:0%
<i> which allows for sharp turns</i>

00:20:24.856 --> 00:20:26.591 line:0%
<i> when chasing prey.</i>

00:20:26.591 --> 00:20:31.129
<i> Life at super speed
 requires fuel, lots of it.</i>

00:20:34.098 --> 00:20:36.568 line:0%
<i> Squid, mackerel, octopus,</i>

00:20:36.568 --> 00:20:40.072 line:0%
<i> and even other tuna
 are all on the menu.</i>

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:45.443 line:0%
<i> To satisfy this
 insatiable hunger,</i>

00:20:45.443 --> 00:20:48.814 line:0%
<i> the yellowfin swim
 nearly 20 miles a day</i>

00:20:48.814 --> 00:20:51.650 line:0%
<i> in search of large
 schools of prey.</i>

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:55.887 line:0%
<i> But here at Ascension,
 the food is on tap.</i>

00:20:55.887 --> 00:21:00.592 line:0%
<i> They track prey by the smell
 of the oil on its skin.</i>

00:21:00.592 --> 00:21:04.195 line:0%
<i> And once spotted,
 the attacks are so fast,</i>

00:21:04.195 --> 00:21:06.831 line:0%
<i> if you blink, you'll miss it.</i>

00:21:06.831 --> 00:21:09.267 line:0%
(music)

00:21:09.267 --> 00:21:15.073 line:0%
(music)

00:21:15.073 --> 00:21:21.012 line:0%
(music)

00:21:21.012 --> 00:21:27.952 line:0%
(music)

00:21:27.952 --> 00:21:34.893 line:0%
(music)

00:21:34.893 --> 00:21:41.833 line:0%
(music)

00:21:41.833 --> 00:21:48.607 line:0%
(music)

00:21:48.607 --> 00:21:51.509 line:0%
<i> Like lions, the tuna
 round up their prey,</i>

00:21:51.509 --> 00:21:53.978 line:0%
<i> making it easier to pick off.</i>

00:21:53.978 --> 00:21:59.050 line:0%
(music)

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:03.088 line:0%
<i> As quickly as it began,
 the frenzy is over.</i>

00:22:05.257 --> 00:22:09.660 line:0%
<i> It takes a thief
 to catch a thief,</i>

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:15.033 line:0%
<i> so who better than
 the fastest shark in the world?</i>

00:22:15.033 --> 00:22:18.069 line:0%
<i> The shortfin mako.</i>

00:22:18.069 --> 00:22:22.874 line:0%
<i> This shark lives life
 in the fast lane, literally.</i>

00:22:22.874 --> 00:22:25.310 line:0%
(music)

00:22:25.310 --> 00:22:30.348 line:0%
(music)

00:22:30.348 --> 00:22:33.818 line:0%
<i> Unable to pump water
 over its gills,</i>

00:22:33.818 --> 00:22:39.224 line:0%
<i> the mako must keep
 moving to stay alive.</i>

00:22:39.224 --> 00:22:42.560 line:0%
<i> In a 30-year lifetime,
 this shark can swim</i>

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:45.664 line:0%
<i> more than 15 times
 around the world.</i>

00:22:47.366 --> 00:22:50.302
<i> It's slightly smaller
 than the tiger shark,</i>

00:22:50.302 --> 00:22:53.871 line:0%
<i> but every inch of this torpedo
 from tip to tail</i>

00:22:53.871 --> 00:22:56.875 line:0%
<i> is evolved for speed.</i>

00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:59.777 line:0%
<i> As heavy as a grizzly,</i>

00:22:59.777 --> 00:23:02.481 line:0%
<i> faster than a jackrabbit.</i>

00:23:06.818 --> 00:23:10.788 line:0%
<i> It roams the vast, open ocean
 at lightning speed</i>

00:23:10.788 --> 00:23:16.227 line:0%
<i> in search of its favorite prey:
 bison-sized tuna.</i>

00:23:16.227 --> 00:23:18.029 line:0%
<i> Like its name suggests,</i>

00:23:18.029 --> 00:23:21.466 line:0%
<i> the shortfin mako has
 short, pointed fins,</i>

00:23:21.466 --> 00:23:25.603 line:0%
<i> which help reduce drag and
 allow for sharp, tight turns,</i>

00:23:25.603 --> 00:23:30.208 line:0%
<i> like a fighter jet, to counter
 the tuna's evasive maneuvers.</i>

00:23:32.343 --> 00:23:36.447 line:0%
<i> Even its narrow, pointed snout
 and long, recurved teeth</i>

00:23:36.447 --> 00:23:40.785 line:0%
<i> are modified for
 hooking prey on the go.</i>

00:23:40.785 --> 00:23:42.853 line:0%
<i> One of the mako's
 key adaptations</i>

00:23:42.853 --> 00:23:47.659 line:0%
<i> for its incredible speed is
 its metallic-looking skin.</i>

00:23:47.659 --> 00:23:51.129 line:0%
<i> Very different than any other
 animal or bony fish,</i>

00:23:51.129 --> 00:23:55.066 line:0%
<i> sharks are covered in thousands
 of tiny, teeth-like scales.</i>

00:23:56.534 --> 00:23:59.503
<i> Hard as granite,
 strong as steel,</i>

00:23:59.503 --> 00:24:01.772
<i> yet flexible like chainmail,</i>

00:24:01.772 --> 00:24:05.977
<i> the mako's scales are smaller
 and lighter than most sharks,</i>

00:24:05.977 --> 00:24:09.681
<i> modified for speed
 rather than protection.</i>

00:24:09.681 --> 00:24:14.553
<i> Each hydrodynamic scale is
 ridged to channel water,</i>

00:24:14.553 --> 00:24:19.657
<i> which in turn reduces
 turbulence and noise.</i>

00:24:19.657 --> 00:24:24.295 line:0%
<i> This shark can freewheel at
 an incredible 35 miles per hour</i>

00:24:24.295 --> 00:24:28.233 line:0%
<i> in near complete silence.</i>

00:24:28.233 --> 00:24:30.201 line:0%
<i> But to catch giant tuna,</i>

00:24:30.201 --> 00:24:34.639 line:0%
<i> the mako must swim faster
 than any other shark.</i>

00:24:34.639 --> 00:24:37.375 line:0%
<i> The secret to
 its explosive speed</i>

00:24:37.375 --> 00:24:41.212 line:0%
<i> is hidden deep within its body.</i>

00:24:41.212 --> 00:24:44.649
<i> Sharks like the tiger are
 powered by swimming muscles</i>

00:24:44.649 --> 00:24:45.883
<i> that run along the sides</i>

00:24:45.883 --> 00:24:47.252
<i> of their bodies,</i>

00:24:47.252 --> 00:24:48.453
<i> producing a slow,</i>

00:24:48.453 --> 00:24:51.723
<i> snakelike movement.</i>

00:24:51.723 --> 00:24:53.925
<i> While in the mako and the tuna,</i>

00:24:53.925 --> 00:24:55.393
<i> these same muscles</i>

00:24:55.393 --> 00:25:00.231
<i> are positioned closer
 to the backbone.</i>

00:25:00.231 --> 00:25:03.902
<i> They act like
 a pair of pistons,</i>

00:25:03.902 --> 00:25:08.105
<i> much like an engine
 for a speedboat propeller.</i>

00:25:08.105 --> 00:25:11.676
<i> These muscles reduce
 the mako's lateral movements</i>

00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:16.314
<i> and focus all the raw power
 directly to its tail.</i>

00:25:20.819 --> 00:25:26.424 line:0%
<i> Even their hydrofoil tails
 are modified for maximum speed.</i>

00:25:26.424 --> 00:25:31.062 line:0%
<i> Unlike most sharks, the mako's
 upper lobe is almost identical</i>

00:25:31.062 --> 00:25:34.699 line:0%
<i> in size and shape
 to the lower lobe.</i>

00:25:34.699 --> 00:25:36.801 line:0%
<i> This allows them
 to catch more water</i>

00:25:36.801 --> 00:25:40.671 line:0%
<i> when swimming, optimizing
 full acceleration.</i>

00:25:40.671 --> 00:25:45.176 line:0%
(music)

00:25:45.176 --> 00:25:47.745 line:0%
<i> So the shortfin mako
 has the raw speed</i>

00:25:47.745 --> 00:25:50.882 line:0%
<i> to ambush the giant tunas,</i>

00:25:50.882 --> 00:25:54.185 line:0%
<i> but the yellowfin
 has a trump card.</i>

00:25:54.185 --> 00:25:56.021 line:0%
<i> It's game on.</i>

00:26:01.893 --> 00:26:04.695 line:0%
<i> Two of the ocean's
 fastest predators</i>

00:26:04.695 --> 00:26:07.465 line:0%
<i> are locked in
 a battle of speed.</i>

00:26:07.465 --> 00:26:12.570 line:0%
(music)

00:26:12.570 --> 00:26:19.109 line:0%
(music)

00:26:19.109 --> 00:26:22.614 line:0%
<i> The mako plays its final hand.</i>

00:26:22.614 --> 00:26:24.883 line:0%
<i> This shark can raise
 its body temperature</i>

00:26:24.883 --> 00:26:29.020 line:0%
<i> 18 degrees above
 that of the water,</i>

00:26:29.020 --> 00:26:31.088 line:0%
<i> increasing its
 hunting abilities,</i>

00:26:31.088 --> 00:26:34.292 line:0%
<i> muscle efficiency and power.</i>

00:26:34.292 --> 00:26:37.161 line:0%
<i> The mako shifts up
 into turbo drive,</i>

00:26:37.161 --> 00:26:40.231 line:0%
<i> closing the gap,</i>

00:26:40.231 --> 00:26:45.002 line:0%
<i> but the tuna has a few tricks
 up its sleeve, too.</i>

00:26:45.002 --> 00:26:46.771 line:0%
<i> In a surprise twist,</i>

00:26:46.771 --> 00:26:50.975 line:0%
<i> everything the mako can do,
 so can the tuna.</i>

00:26:50.975 --> 00:26:52.643 line:0%
<i> Through convergent evolution,</i>

00:26:52.643 --> 00:26:56.814 line:0%
<i> the yellowfin is also optimized
 to hunt at speed.</i>

00:26:56.814 --> 00:26:58.249 line:0%
<i> Just like the mako,</i>

00:26:58.249 --> 00:27:00.418 line:0%
<i> the tuna's torpedo-shaped body</i>

00:27:00.418 --> 00:27:01.652 line:0%
<i> is also coated with</i>

00:27:01.652 --> 00:27:04.154
<i> small scales to reduce drag,</i>

00:27:04.154 --> 00:27:06.290 line:0%
<i> and its short, pointed fins</i>

00:27:06.290 --> 00:27:07.592 line:0%
<i> also allow for sharp,</i>

00:27:07.592 --> 00:27:10.127 line:0%
<i> evasive maneuvers.</i>

00:27:10.127 --> 00:27:12.930
<i> The tuna also has modified
 swimming muscles</i>

00:27:12.930 --> 00:27:16.801
<i> to minimize body movement
 and provide maximum power</i>

00:27:16.801 --> 00:27:20.071 line:0%
<i> to a similar
 near-symmetrical tail.</i>

00:27:20.071 --> 00:27:21.805 line:0%
<i> And like the mako,</i>

00:27:21.805 --> 00:27:23.674 line:0%
<i> the tuna can warm its blood</i>

00:27:23.674 --> 00:27:27.311 line:0%
<i> to turbocharge its muscles.</i>

00:27:27.311 --> 00:27:30.047 line:0%
<i> Mako meets its match.</i>

00:27:30.047 --> 00:27:35.753 line:0%
(music)

00:27:35.753 --> 00:27:38.857 line:0%
<i> On paper, the mako
 has the speed,</i>

00:27:38.857 --> 00:27:41.258 line:0%
<i> but the overwhelming
 numbers of tuna</i>

00:27:41.258 --> 00:27:44.095 line:0%
<i> create distraction
 in the chase.</i>

00:27:46.097 --> 00:27:51.969 line:0%
<i> Unable to lock on to a target,
 the mako steps off the gas.</i>

00:27:51.969 --> 00:27:57.074 line:0%
<i> Like Houdini,
 the tunas escape once again,</i>

00:27:57.074 --> 00:28:00.111 line:0%
<i> and the mako folds.</i>

00:28:04.882 --> 00:28:08.452 line:0%
<i> This elusive super fish gives
 the sharks of Ascension</i>

00:28:08.452 --> 00:28:12.624 line:0%
<i> a run for their money.</i>

00:28:12.624 --> 00:28:19.096 line:0%
<i> But there is one threat
 the tuna cannot escape from...</i>

00:28:19.096 --> 00:28:23.401 line:0%
<i> a predator that doesn't
 play by the rules...</i>

00:28:23.401 --> 00:28:25.036 line:0%
<i> man.</i>

00:28:26.870 --> 00:28:29.173 line:0%
<i> Although yellowfin
 are near threatened,</i>

00:28:29.173 --> 00:28:31.509 line:0%
<i> they remain
 a highly prized catch,</i>

00:28:31.509 --> 00:28:35.380 line:0%
<i> both commercially
 and for sport.</i>

00:28:35.380 --> 00:28:38.115 line:0%
<i> Anglers, spearfishermen
 and trophy hunters</i>

00:28:38.115 --> 00:28:39.818 line:0%
<i> from all around the world</i>

00:28:39.818 --> 00:28:43.921 line:0%
<i> believe that giant yellowfin
 are, pound for pound,</i>

00:28:43.921 --> 00:28:47.892 line:0%
<i> the fastest and strongest
 of all big game tunas.</i>

00:28:51.028 --> 00:28:53.664 line:0%
<i> But it takes
 ingenuity, patience,</i>

00:28:53.664 --> 00:28:56.734 line:0%
<i> and sheer luck to land one.</i>

00:28:56.734 --> 00:28:59.904 line:0%
<i> Such a formidable predator
 has gained the respect</i>

00:28:59.904 --> 00:29:01.906 line:0%
<i> and honor of battle,</i>

00:29:01.906 --> 00:29:06.143 line:0%
<i> and each year more and more
 fishermen arrive at Ascension</i>

00:29:06.143 --> 00:29:10.448 line:0%
<i> stealing the tuna from
 right under the sharks' noses.</i>

00:29:14.686 --> 00:29:20.191 line:0%
<i> It can take eons for animals
 to learn new behaviors,</i>

00:29:20.191 --> 00:29:25.463 line:0%
<i> but more intelligent creatures
 can adapt much faster,</i>

00:29:25.463 --> 00:29:28.900 line:0%
<i> sometimes within just
 a few generations.</i>

00:29:31.569 --> 00:29:36.141 line:0%
<i> One such species is
 the Galapagos sharks.</i>

00:29:36.141 --> 00:29:38.776 line:0%
<i> Experts believe these
 resourceful predators</i>

00:29:38.776 --> 00:29:41.746 line:0%
<i> have learned to make
 a crucial connection</i>

00:29:41.746 --> 00:29:46.951 line:0%
<i> between the giant tuna
 and the fishing boats.</i>

00:29:46.951 --> 00:29:49.787 line:0%
<i> The Galapagos may not be
 as fast as the mako</i>

00:29:49.787 --> 00:29:52.189 line:0%
<i> or as strong as the tiger,</i>

00:29:52.189 --> 00:29:56.827 line:0%
<i> but this dangerously smart
 predator has a hunting hack,</i>

00:29:56.827 --> 00:30:00.665 line:0%
<i> and they plan to use man
 to help them out.</i>

00:30:02.966 --> 00:30:05.536 line:0%
<i> Man is a creature of habit,</i>

00:30:05.536 --> 00:30:10.975 line:0%
<i> and fishermen always do
 the same thing every day.</i>

00:30:10.975 --> 00:30:14.378 line:0%
<i> They head out at the same time.</i>

00:30:14.378 --> 00:30:16.481 line:0%
<i> They use the same bait.</i>

00:30:19.049 --> 00:30:23.120 line:0%
<i> And select the same lures.</i>

00:30:23.120 --> 00:30:26.524 line:0%
<i> They trawl the same
 successful spots,</i>

00:30:26.524 --> 00:30:30.328 line:0%
<i> targeting the exact fish
 that the sharks yearn for.</i>

00:30:32.964 --> 00:30:36.534 line:0%
<i> Day after day, the inquisitive
 Galapagos sharks</i>

00:30:36.534 --> 00:30:38.970 line:0%
<i> take advantage of this monotony</i>

00:30:38.970 --> 00:30:41.939 line:0%
<i> and start
 to learn the patterns.</i>

00:30:41.939 --> 00:30:47.378 line:0%
(music)

00:30:47.378 --> 00:30:53.684 line:0%
(music)

00:30:53.684 --> 00:30:57.589 line:0%
<i> Like a hive mind, they begin
 to associate triggers,</i>

00:30:57.589 --> 00:31:01.859 line:0%
<i> sight, sounds and smells
 of struggling fish.</i>

00:31:01.859 --> 00:31:06.531 line:0%
(music)

00:31:06.531 --> 00:31:08.332 line:0%
<i> The hum of a boat motor,</i>

00:31:08.332 --> 00:31:10.334 line:0%
<i> the scent of bait in the water,</i>

00:31:10.334 --> 00:31:13.137 line:0%
<i> or even the snap
 of a speargun's elastic</i>

00:31:13.137 --> 00:31:16.640 line:0%
<i> means it's time to feed.</i>

00:31:16.640 --> 00:31:18.075 line:0%
<i> The sharks work out</i>

00:31:18.075 --> 00:31:20.644 line:0%
<i> that 20 minutes
 after a boat arrives,</i>

00:31:20.644 --> 00:31:23.748 line:0%
<i> a fish is usually on the line.</i>

00:31:23.748 --> 00:31:28.019 line:0%
<i> Forget Pavlov's dogs;
 meet Pavlov's sharks.</i>

00:31:30.054 --> 00:31:34.359 line:0%
<i> Some fishermen will do anything
 to cash in on a yellowfin,</i>

00:31:34.359 --> 00:31:40.031 line:0%
<i> and the bigger the risk,
 the bigger the reward.</i>

00:31:40.031 --> 00:31:44.335 line:0%
<i> But entering these waters
 could cost you your life.</i>

00:31:48.139 --> 00:31:50.874 line:0%
(music)

00:31:50.874 --> 00:31:57.247 line:0%
<i> Miles out to sea,
 this spearfisherman is alone...</i>

00:31:57.247 --> 00:31:59.751 line:0%
<i> or so he thinks.</i>

00:32:01.986 --> 00:32:06.524 line:0%
<i> He baits the water to draw
 the yellowfin up from the deep.</i>

00:32:06.524 --> 00:32:13.497 line:0%
(music)

00:32:13.497 --> 00:32:17.868 line:0%
<i> But this free food doesn't
 only attract the tuna.</i>

00:32:17.868 --> 00:32:21.305 line:0%
(music)

00:32:21.305 --> 00:32:27.544 line:0%
(music)

00:32:27.544 --> 00:32:33.150 line:0%
<i> Several miles away, a pack of
 hungry Galapagos smell it, too.</i>

00:32:33.150 --> 00:32:35.786 line:0%
(music)

00:32:35.786 --> 00:32:42.226 line:0%
(music)

00:32:42.226 --> 00:32:48.232 line:0%
(music)

00:32:48.232 --> 00:32:50.100 line:0%
<i> With chum in the water,</i>

00:32:50.100 --> 00:32:54.605 line:0%
<i> the diver knows he only has
 a short window of opportunity</i>

00:32:54.605 --> 00:32:58.241 line:0%
<i> before the sharks find him.</i>

00:32:58.241 --> 00:33:00.945 line:0%
<i> Every minute he stays here,</i>

00:33:00.945 --> 00:33:04.248 line:0%
<i> the more he puts
 his life at risk.</i>

00:33:04.248 --> 00:33:10.888 line:0%
(music)

00:33:10.888 --> 00:33:13.324 line:0%
(music)

00:33:13.324 --> 00:33:18.662 line:0%
(music)

00:33:18.662 --> 00:33:20.831 line:0%
<i> Who will arrive first?</i>

00:33:20.831 --> 00:33:25.269 line:0%
(music)

00:33:25.269 --> 00:33:29.006 line:0%
<i> Tuna?</i>

00:33:29.006 --> 00:33:31.209 line:0%
<i> Or sharks?</i>

00:33:38.882 --> 00:33:42.786 line:0%
(music)

00:33:42.786 --> 00:33:45.522 line:0%
<i> Dark shapes appear below.</i>

00:33:45.522 --> 00:33:50.661 line:0%
(music)

00:33:50.661 --> 00:33:56.333 line:0%
(music)

00:33:56.333 --> 00:34:00.505 line:0%
<i> It's the yellowfin,
 and they're big.</i>

00:34:04.108 --> 00:34:06.677 line:0%
<i> They won't hang around
 for long.</i>

00:34:06.677 --> 00:34:11.449 line:0%
(music)

00:34:11.449 --> 00:34:13.917 line:0%
<i> Should he risk it?</i>

00:34:13.917 --> 00:34:19.323 line:0%
(music)

00:34:19.323 --> 00:34:23.561 line:0%
(music)

00:34:23.561 --> 00:34:27.765 line:0%
<i> One good-sized tuna could
 pay the bills for a year.</i>

00:34:27.765 --> 00:34:33.570 line:0%
(music)

00:34:33.570 --> 00:34:40.044 line:0%
(music)

00:34:40.044 --> 00:34:42.713 line:0%
<i> The tuna may be big,</i>

00:34:42.713 --> 00:34:46.517 line:0%
<i> but they're so fast,
 he can't get a clean shot.</i>

00:34:46.517 --> 00:34:51.689 line:0%
(music)

00:34:51.689 --> 00:34:54.358 line:0%
<i> The longer the diver
 stays in the water,</i>

00:34:54.358 --> 00:34:58.729 line:0%
<i> the more chance the hunter
 may become the hunted.</i>

00:34:58.729 --> 00:35:01.165 line:0%
(music)

00:35:01.165 --> 00:35:06.037 line:0%
(music)

00:35:06.037 --> 00:35:07.805 line:0%
<i> He lines up.</i>

00:35:19.950 --> 00:35:22.653 line:0%
<i> A direct hit.</i>

00:35:22.653 --> 00:35:24.555 line:0%
<i> The tuna dives.</i>

00:35:27.124 --> 00:35:31.462 line:0%
<i> Now he's fighting
 a 200-pound lump of muscle.</i>

00:35:31.462 --> 00:35:33.864 line:0%
<i> His second spear just
 seems to enrage</i>

00:35:33.864 --> 00:35:36.534 line:0%
<i> the powerful fish further.</i>

00:35:40.270 --> 00:35:42.372 line:0%
<i> The more
 the yellowfin struggles,</i>

00:35:42.372 --> 00:35:47.378 line:0%
<i> the clearer the signal is
 to the sharks:</i>

00:35:47.378 --> 00:35:49.680 line:0%
<i> Food is served.</i>

00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:52.116 line:0%
(music)

00:35:52.116 --> 00:35:57.053 line:0%
(music)

00:35:57.053 --> 00:35:59.657 line:0%
<i> The spearfisherman must hurry,</i>

00:35:59.657 --> 00:36:03.260 line:0%
<i> but this tuna shows
 no signs of tiring.</i>

00:36:03.260 --> 00:36:09.600 line:0%
(music)

00:36:09.600 --> 00:36:16.240 line:0%
(music)

00:36:16.240 --> 00:36:17.808 line:0%
<i> Too late.</i>

00:36:17.808 --> 00:36:22.246 line:0%
<i> The first wave
 of Galapagos arrives.</i>

00:36:22.246 --> 00:36:23.814 line:0%
<i> They want the tuna,</i>

00:36:23.814 --> 00:36:26.950 line:0%
<i> and will happily go
 through man to get it.</i>

00:36:26.950 --> 00:36:32.689 line:0%
(music)

00:36:32.689 --> 00:36:39.129 line:0%
(music)

00:36:39.129 --> 00:36:46.070 line:0%
(music)

00:36:46.070 --> 00:36:49.840 line:0%
<i> The more it struggles, the more
 excited the sharks become.</i>

00:36:49.840 --> 00:36:55.045 line:0%
(music)

00:36:55.045 --> 00:37:01.485 line:0%
(music)

00:37:01.485 --> 00:37:08.058 line:0%
(music)

00:37:08.058 --> 00:37:14.998 line:0%
(music)

00:37:14.998 --> 00:37:21.972 line:0%
(music)

00:37:21.972 --> 00:37:23.240 line:0%
(man yells)

00:37:23.240 --> 00:37:28.111 line:0%
(music)

00:37:28.111 --> 00:37:34.151 line:0%
<i> The spearfisherman escapes
 with his tuna and his life.</i>

00:37:34.151 --> 00:37:35.753 line:0%
<i> The hungry sharks are left</i>

00:37:35.753 --> 00:37:40.157 line:0%
<i> with nothing but the scraps
 of his bait bag.</i>

00:37:40.157 --> 00:37:43.393 line:0%
<i> Perhaps it was this
 distraction of free food</i>

00:37:43.393 --> 00:37:46.163 line:0%
<i> or that only a handful
 of sharks arrived</i>

00:37:46.163 --> 00:37:49.566 line:0%
<i> that enabled the diver's
 lucky escape.</i>

00:37:49.566 --> 00:37:52.002 line:0%
(music)

00:37:52.002 --> 00:37:56.707 line:0%
(music)

00:37:56.707 --> 00:38:00.978 line:0%
<i> The fishermen have yet
 to hook a giant tuna.</i>

00:38:00.978 --> 00:38:04.948 line:0%
<i> It's too dangerous to
 get back in the water.</i>

00:38:04.948 --> 00:38:09.520 line:0%
<i> The only safe way to catch one
 is from the boat.</i>

00:38:12.856 --> 00:38:14.424 line:0%
<i> Could this be the opportunity</i>

00:38:14.424 --> 00:38:18.696 line:0%
<i> the sharks have been
 waiting for?</i>

00:38:18.696 --> 00:38:21.899 line:0%
<i> For the Galapagos,
 it's double or nothing.</i>

00:38:28.339 --> 00:38:32.576 line:0%
<i> It's the end of July,
 and the giant tuna are here.</i>

00:38:32.576 --> 00:38:35.145 line:0%
<i> These yellowfins
 are super fast,</i>

00:38:35.145 --> 00:38:39.983 line:0%
<i> immensely strong and can grow
 to well over 800 pounds,</i>

00:38:39.983 --> 00:38:42.987 line:0%
<i> making them even
 harder to catch.</i>

00:38:42.987 --> 00:38:45.823 line:0%
<i> They are what everyone wants.</i>

00:38:48.993 --> 00:38:53.230 line:0%
<i> For man, a giant yellowfin is
 worth thousands of dollars</i>

00:38:53.230 --> 00:38:56.700 line:0%
<i> and one of the ultimate
 fishing trophies.</i>

00:38:56.700 --> 00:39:00.037 line:0%
<i> For the sharks that traveled
 all the way to Ascension,</i>

00:39:00.037 --> 00:39:04.041 line:0%
<i> the giant tuna is
 their meal ticket home.</i>

00:39:04.041 --> 00:39:09.446 line:0%
<i> Ascension is now
 the perfect storm of predators.</i>

00:39:09.446 --> 00:39:12.216 line:0%
<i> But who will win?</i>

00:39:12.216 --> 00:39:15.019 line:0%
<i> The enormous tiger shark
 is just too slow</i>

00:39:15.019 --> 00:39:17.988 line:0%
<i> to step up to the plate.</i>

00:39:17.988 --> 00:39:21.458 line:0%
<i> The mako may have supreme
 speed and agility,</i>

00:39:21.458 --> 00:39:25.863 line:0%
<i> but so does the giant tuna.</i>

00:39:25.863 --> 00:39:29.332 line:0%
<i> It's the Galapagos mob
 that has the best chance</i>

00:39:29.332 --> 00:39:31.735 line:0%
<i> of a successful hunt.</i>

00:39:31.735 --> 00:39:33.904 line:0%
<i> A shark is dangerous enough,</i>

00:39:33.904 --> 00:39:37.408 line:0%
<i> but an intelligent shark
 is deadly.</i>

00:39:39.710 --> 00:39:42.779 line:0%
<i> The Galapagos is
 smart on its own,</i>

00:39:42.779 --> 00:39:47.685 line:0%
<i> and here at Ascension,
 there are thousands of them.</i>

00:39:47.685 --> 00:39:53.557 line:0%
<i> This is their domain,
 and it's time to take it back.</i>

00:39:56.426 --> 00:40:01.031 line:0%
<i> Most flee and hide from
 the approaching fishermen,</i>

00:40:01.031 --> 00:40:05.369 line:0%
<i> but for the clever Galapagos,
 it's a dinner bell.</i>

00:40:05.369 --> 00:40:09.906 line:0%
(music)

00:40:09.906 --> 00:40:16.280 line:0%
(music)

00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:19.215 line:0%
<i> Lures are rigged,
 the lines are set.</i>

00:40:19.215 --> 00:40:21.652 line:0%
<i> It's a waiting game for all.</i>

00:40:21.652 --> 00:40:28.191 line:0%
(music)

00:40:28.191 --> 00:40:30.661 line:0%
<i> Shapes appear in the deep.</i>

00:40:30.661 --> 00:40:36.066 line:0%
(music)

00:40:36.066 --> 00:40:42.138 line:0%
(music)

00:40:42.138 --> 00:40:44.608 line:0%
<i> A giant tuna takes the bait.</i>

00:40:44.608 --> 00:40:51.014 line:0%
(music)

00:40:51.014 --> 00:40:53.450 line:0%
(music)

00:40:53.450 --> 00:40:58.922 line:0%
(music)

00:40:58.922 --> 00:41:05.962 line:0%
(music)

00:41:05.962 --> 00:41:12.735 line:0%
(music)

00:41:12.735 --> 00:41:16.507 line:0%
<i> The dinner bell is ringing.</i>

00:41:16.507 --> 00:41:18.675 line:0%
<i> It's like the wahoo massacre,</i>

00:41:18.675 --> 00:41:22.245 line:0%
<i> but this meal is as big
 as some of the sharks.</i>

00:41:22.245 --> 00:41:27.484 line:0%
(music)

00:41:27.484 --> 00:41:30.687 line:0%
<i> The giant yellowfin
 begins to tire.</i>

00:41:30.687 --> 00:41:33.958 line:0%
<i> The first Galapagos moves in.</i>

00:41:37.394 --> 00:41:40.230 line:0%
<i> For the fishermen, it's a race
 to get the prize catch</i>

00:41:40.230 --> 00:41:42.766 line:0%
<i> onto the safety of the boat.</i>

00:41:46.603 --> 00:41:48.638 line:0%
<i> But the tuna is too strong.</i>

00:41:48.638 --> 00:41:51.074 line:0%
(music)

00:41:51.074 --> 00:41:56.446 line:0%
(music)

00:41:56.446 --> 00:41:59.116 line:0%
<i> The Galapagos start to swarm.</i>

00:41:59.116 --> 00:42:04.387 line:0%
(music)

00:42:04.387 --> 00:42:09.826 line:0%
(music)

00:42:09.826 --> 00:42:16.733 line:0%
(music)

00:42:16.733 --> 00:42:23.707 line:0%
(music)

00:42:23.707 --> 00:42:30.180 line:0%
(music)

00:42:30.180 --> 00:42:33.417 line:0%
<i> One dominant shark
 gets the first taste.</i>

00:42:41.258 --> 00:42:44.728 line:0%
<i> Thick, warm blood will
 attract the masses.</i>

00:42:45.829 --> 00:42:47.631
<i> Covering the shark's snout</i>

00:42:47.631 --> 00:42:52.035
<i> are thousands of what
 appear to be blackheads,</i>

00:42:52.035 --> 00:42:55.205
<i> but they're really like
 built-in volt meters</i>

00:42:55.205 --> 00:42:58.075
<i> picking up the minute
 electrical signature</i>

00:42:58.075 --> 00:43:00.944
<i> and even the heartbeat of prey.</i>

00:43:00.944 --> 00:43:04.848
<i> This sixth sense is
 the most acute sensory system</i>

00:43:04.848 --> 00:43:07.685
<i> in the animal kingdom.</i>

00:43:07.685 --> 00:43:11.221 line:0%
<i> The salt from the tuna's blood
 increases the intensity</i>

00:43:11.221 --> 00:43:14.892 line:0%
<i> of the electrical field
 surrounding the fish,</i>

00:43:14.892 --> 00:43:18.629 line:0%
<i> which is why a shark will
 continue to target and attack</i>

00:43:18.629 --> 00:43:20.998 line:0%
<i> only the injured victim.</i>

00:43:26.303 --> 00:43:31.107 line:0%
<i> Excitement soon
 turns to frenzy.</i>

00:43:31.107 --> 00:43:34.377 line:0%
<i> Tuna is survival
 to the Galapagos shark.</i>

00:43:34.377 --> 00:43:37.981 line:0%
(music)

00:43:37.981 --> 00:43:43.420 line:0%
(music)

00:43:43.420 --> 00:43:47.992 line:0%
(music)

00:43:50.227 --> 00:43:55.399 line:0%
<i> In less than a minute,
 a 350-pound fish vanishes.</i>

00:43:57.201 --> 00:44:02.705 line:0%
<i> The fishermen leave with
 nothing but a broken line.</i>

00:44:02.705 --> 00:44:06.910 line:0%
<i> The Galapagos sharks
 rule The Rock.</i>

